    {
      "id": "shifted-subset-sum",
      "root": "../../../../examples/scalability/shifted-subset-sum",
      "entry": "subset_sum.lp",
      "sha256": "366ed74d26e462b7f1fc02fc73bf4891daa1843b71a7351b01c8e5c137e627de",
      "contract": {
        "satisfiability": "unsat",
        "family": "all",
        "model_count": 0,
        "cost": null,
        "witnesses": [],
        "required_symbols": [],
        "notes": [
          "At n=8 the weights are 9..16. No singleton reaches 17 and the smallest pair weighs 19.",
          "More generally target=2*n+1 is unattainable; target=2*n+3 selects exactly items 1 and 2 for n>=2."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "two-qbf",
      "root": "../../../../examples/scalability/two-qbf",
      "entry": "two_qbf.lp",
      "sha256": "c9dc3cf1c650fae86a0d7fa5827c531a8b415eb3dfdcd200cfef47a8dbed7e44",
      "contract": {
        "satisfiability": "sat",
        "family": "all",
        "model_count": 2,
        "cost": null,
        "witnesses": [
          [
            "nx(1)",
            "nx(2)",
            "nx(3)"
          ],
          [
            "nx(3)",
            "x(1)",
            "x(2)"
          ]
        ],
        "required_symbols": [],
        "notes": [
          "Three existential and eight universal variables; 68 terms, each one existential and three universal literals; seed 1. Two existential assignments make the formula hold for every universal assignment.",
          "Every answer set is saturated, so membership needs the complete check that no universal assignment falsifies the formula: the frozen reduct's proper-subset query, which the frozen-positive certificate declines."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "two-qbf-parity",
      "root": "../../../../examples/scalability/two-qbf-parity",
      "entry": "two_qbf_parity.lp",
      "sha256": "2c3a862dabf858f0f017083a3c6753cf97fb33a7d69092817a451b78f98ff3ea",
      "contract": {
        "satisfiability": "sat",
        "family": "all",
        "model_count": 1,
        "cost": null,
        "witnesses": [
          [
            "nx(1)",
            "nx(2)"
          ]
        ],
        "required_symbols": [],
        "notes": [
          "Two existential variables; the core is a parity contradiction over n=6 inputs, computed by two chains of three-variable exclusive-or gates (16 universal variables, 42 clauses); seed 1 orders the second chain. The first existential assignment gets the whole contradiction, the other three lose one clause each.",
          "Every answer set is saturated, so membership needs the complete check that no universal assignment satisfies its core: the frozen reduct's proper-subset query. At n=16 the stable candidate's query walks about 131,000 regions."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "two-qbf-tseitin",
      "root": "../../../../examples/scalability/two-qbf-tseitin",
      "entry": "two_qbf_tseitin.lp",
      "sha256": "7c18fe0f648b6d74ba4979e691d5e73ecd2e4074365da199fdef0f8f0710ad5b",
      "contract": {
        "satisfiability": "sat",
        "family": "all",
        "model_count": 1,
        "cost": null,
        "witnesses": [
          [
            "nx(1)",
            "nx(2)"
          ]
        ],
        "required_symbols": [],
        "notes": [
          "Two existential variables; the core is Tseitin's parity formula on the committed 3-regular graph on 12 vertices (18 universal variables, 48 clauses) with an odd total charge. The first existential assignment gets the whole contradiction, the other three lose one clause each.",
          "Every answer set is saturated, so membership needs the complete check that no universal assignment satisfies its core: the frozen reduct's proper-subset query. On 24 vertices the subset queries walk about 56,000 regions."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "two-qbf-pigeonhole",
      "root": "../../../../examples/scalability/two-qbf-pigeonhole",
      "entry": "two_qbf_pigeonhole.lp",
      "sha256": "4de3da43035196cf7f37e5ba17222ceba22d019e223eb6e682c450a8dd6a0c7f",
      "contract": {
        "satisfiability": "sat",
